    "reasoning": "I is false because tangent's vertical asymptotes occur at x=\\frac{\\pi}{2}+n\\pi, while x=n\\pi gives zeros. II is true because tangent has period \\pi, so adding 2n\\pi preserves its value wherever defined. III is false because tangent's range is all real numbers. Thus \"II only\", current option \"0\", agrees with the earlier answer and the captured Math Academy solution's three truth judgments.",
